# Milne, Class Field Theory, Lemma II.1.37

For a `G`-module `A`, let `A_*` be the coinduced module of functions `G → A` and embed `A` by
`a ↦ (g ↦ g • a)`.  After forgetting the `G`-action, evaluation at `1` retracts this embedding.
